
<p>Matthew Butterick:</p>

<blockquote>
  <p>So let’s not take the bait. Nor overcomplicate. We needn’t spin
our collective wheels spitballing answers to big-picture,
long-term Al-policy questions. We don’t know enough yet. The best
next steps are the concrete ones: Big Al needs to follow all
current laws — just like everyone else. So far — they haven’t.
When Big Al breaks those laws, they must face prosecution and
penalties — just like everyone else. So far — they haven’t. The
state and federal agencies tasked with enforcing those laws need
to apply them to Big Al — just like everyone else. So far — they
haven’t. In short, we have to attend to the basic features of the
rule of law. So far — we haven’t. If we can’t or won’t insist on
that now, then we shouldn’t expect to be able to later.</p>
</blockquote>

